\date{\today}
\maketitle

\section{Abstract}
The current study investigates the effectiveness of hormone therapy in treating infertility in women. It gives a detailed account of a commonly used method, clomiphene citrate.

\section{Proposed Method}
Hormone therapy plays a critical role in the management of female infertility. One of the majorly used drugs, clomiphene citrate modulates the action of gonadotropins. It blocks estrogen receptors inhibiting negative feedback and causing increased production of FSH and LH.

\section{Result and Discussion}
Previous studies show promising results in the use of clomiphene citrate for patients with polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS) to promote ovulation. The mechanism of action involves the increased production of gonadotropins that stimulate follicular growth.

\section{Conclusion}
This study concluded that the hormone therapy, particularly clomiphene citrate, has increased fertility probability in females who fail to ovulate spontaneously.

\end{document}
```

